questions.question_text:
The brightness of a glow stick was measured each hour.
The points and the fitted curve are shown.
Which model gives the brightness $y$ after $x$ hours?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=8.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.4,xmax=4.6,ymin=-5,ymax=92,xtick={0,1,...,4},ytick={0,10,...,90},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$ (hours)},ylabel={Brightness},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:4.2,samples=100] {80*exp(x*ln(0.5))};
\addplot[only marks,mark=*,black] coordinates {(0,80) (1,40) (2,20) (3,10)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
